      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual maximum adult dose of 4 g/day. Even with normal liver function, that amount risks acute liver failure. A single 5 g dose is also above the standard 1 g maximum per administration, and it's near the range where toxicity is a concern for a 70 kg patient.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours** (1.95\u20132.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day), or four times daily for 4 g/day, which is the ceiling\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 5,000 mg TID is what you want, tell me the clinical reason. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
