     "type": "message",
     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 15 g/day it could cause serious liver injury or death. I don't know of any clinical scenario where it would be appropriate, and I can't make it safe by adding a note.\n\nYou have other ways to get what you need:\n\n- **If you meant a different dose,** give me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. The maximum is 1,000 mg per dose and 4 g/day, or less if risk factors apply.\n- **If there's an unusual clinical reason,** such as a protocol or research setting, please go through pharmacy and your institution's override process. A pharmacist can review it and document it properly.\n- **If acetaminophen has been ingested in excess,** that is an overdose. It needs poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US), an acetaminophen level, and consideration of N-acetylcysteine. It doesn't need a new order.\n\nI'm glad to enter an alternative analgesic regimen if that helps."
      }
     ],
